{
 "_doc": "Forest set piece, round 4 (ADR-0053; tier 2, site forest: a dry ravine). An abandoned logging line: a timber trestle (kit deck room D on level 1 over the ravine, its sides open, the w4_trestle_bent props standing under it) runs from a cribbed embankment into a tunnel (kit rooms T two storeys tall with rock walls on the w4_trestle_hill plinth, the w4_trestle_tunnel_portal on its face) whose far end the Cordon blew. Level 0 holds the watchman's shack, the section tool house and the creek bed under the rotten deck boards (a kit room with open sides so the weak floor drops into it). Route: the embankment stair (its gate bolted from the deck) -> the tool house side door (the section hands; the niche key on the board) -> the watchman's shack through its smashed window (the bulkhead key) -> the ravine (jaws) -> the ladder up a bent (climbed, no hatch) -> the deck (rotten boards) -> the Cordon's chained bulkhead -> cans in the mouth wake the train crew -> the boxcar (vault in at the door: freight, the fireman's letter) -> the padlocked refuge niche: Hank the engineer (guardian) and the stores -> back along the deck, unbolt the gate, down the stair.",
