   "population": "loggers",
   "story": "The logging line's work train went into Tunnel 2 on a Monday to clear a slide at the far portal: Engine 4, a flat of cribbing logs and the tool boxcar, Hank Tollefsen at the throttle. The Cordon had told the section foreman to hold all work; the slide would not wait. At eleven the Cordon blew the far portal to close the grade as a road out of the quarantine, and the hill came down on the engine. That evening a Cordon crew framed a bulkhead across the near portal with the train still inside, chained it, and gave the trestle watchman the key and orders never to open it. The crew knocked on the boards for a week. Hank, cut and feverish, had them padlock him in the refuge niche with the stores. The section hands shut themselves in the tool house with the fever, and the watchman nailed his own door and sat by his stove so he would not hear the knocking.",
